BeeAI Agentic Lab
=================

This project is a refactored and reorganized version of the hands-on lab
"Building Agentic AI Systems with the BeeAI Framework", published by
IBM Skills Network as part of the IBM RAG and Agentic AI Professional
Certificate.

  Original lab author: Wojciech "Victor" Fulmyk
  Original lab code and guide: © IBM Corporation. All rights reserved.
  The lab content is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The original lab scripts (t1.py - t12.py) are included unmodified in the
`original_lab/` directory for reference. All agent designs, prompts, sample
queries, schemas and the calculator tool originate from that lab.

Changes made in this version (Apache 2.0, section 4(b)):
  - Split the twelve standalone scripts into a Python package with separate
    modules for configuration, model creation, prompts, schemas, tools,
    agents and runnable examples.
  - Replaced six near-duplicate agent scripts (t5-t10) with one
    configurable builder and reusable requirement sets.
  - Added a command-line interface, `.env` support, error hints, and tests.
  - Replaced the calculator's `eval` with an AST-based evaluator and made the
    prompt template tolerate literal braces.
  - Applied the lab's model defaults at run time instead of in a separate
    `t1.py` process.

This project depends on the BeeAI Framework (https://github.com/i-am-bee/beeai-framework),
an open-source project under the Linux Foundation AI & Data, licensed under
Apache 2.0.
